    "result_text": "All tests pass. The full suite (the acceptance tests are the only test classes in the project) is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI converted owner deletion to a soft-delete. Changes:\n\n**Domain / persistence**\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added a `deleted` boolean column (`@Column(name = \"deleted\")`), defaulting to `false` for new owners, with getter/setter.\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added a `deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE` column to the `owners` table. (Tests run against hsqldb, the app against h2; mysql/postgres updated for parity.)\n\n**API contract**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` boolean property to the `Owner` response schema, so `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns it (MapStruct maps it automatically by name; no mapper change needed).\n\n**Endpoint behavior**\n- `rest/function/owner/DeleteOwner.java` \u2014 now flags `owner.setDeleted(true)` and `save`s the record instead of removing it. The DELETE pipeline still ends in `RespondWithNoContent` (204, a 2xx), and the row is retained so `GET` still returns the owner.\n- `CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique.java` (the blocking household-duplicate check), `FlagOwnerPossibleDuplicate.java`, and `CountOwnerNamesakes.java` \u2014 each now skips owners flagged deleted, so a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only matching owner has been soft-deleted.\n\n**Verification** \u2014 `./mvnw -o test`: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`, covering both new acceptance tests (`coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains`, `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck`).",
